{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01002",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 4.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I've settled them in, ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.49,
      "end_seconds": 12.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.49,
      "end_seconds": 21.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "It's a fluttering in my chest. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.97,
      "end_seconds": 25.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.74,
      "end_seconds": 30.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Hmm, it's been six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.79,
      "end_seconds": 35.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Okay, how much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.12,
      "end_seconds": 37.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.82,
      "end_seconds": 41.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Sure. Any your heart racing as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.18,
      "end_seconds": 57.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.13,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, yeah. Three weeks, I'd say. With my heart racing, it's a few times a day. I've been feeling anxious during it too, for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.62,
      "end_seconds": 79.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, weight loss, fainting or sweating?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.62,
      "end_seconds": 89.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "Ah, uh, I haven't had chest pain, weight loss, fainting or sweating, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.62,
      "end_seconds": 94.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Yes. What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.45,
      "end_seconds": 98.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.08,
      "end_seconds": 103.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.95,
      "end_seconds": 110.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Plasters. I come out in... well, a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.74,
      "end_seconds": 115.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.18,
      "end_seconds": 120.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Actually, no, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.06,
      "end_seconds": 129.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.54,
      "end_seconds": 132.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.71,
      "end_seconds": 136.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.28,
      "end_seconds": 143.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.81,
      "end_seconds": 147.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.69,
      "end_seconds": 153.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.09,
      "end_seconds": 156.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.72,
      "end_seconds": 163.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.7,
      "end_seconds": 170.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.66,
      "end_seconds": 181.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "I, I take Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I take amlodipine, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.76,
      "end_seconds": 185.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.85,
      "end_seconds": 187.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.33,
      "end_seconds": 191.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Sure. Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.57,
      "end_seconds": 199.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.08,
      "end_seconds": 201.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.88,
      "end_seconds": 205.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Yes, an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.79,
      "end_seconds": 207.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.37,
      "end_seconds": 215.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.1,
      "end_seconds": 222.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes and an underactive thyroid, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 230.97,
      "end_seconds": 238.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature is 36.6 degrees, pulse 118, BP is 133 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.74,
      "end_seconds": 240.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.27,
      "end_seconds": 247.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.3,
      "end_seconds": 251.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.8,
      "end_seconds": 267.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal with no murmur."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.71,
      "end_seconds": 282.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "You can relax now. Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with paroxysmal palpitations, possibly an atrial arrhythmia at this stage. Anxiety-related palpitations is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.86,
      "end_seconds": 288.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Well, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.44,
      "end_seconds": 310.03,
      "duration_seconds": 20.59,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's paroxysmal palpitations, possibly an atrial arrhythmia, and we'll know more once the a thyroid test is back. Let's book a thyroid test to look into palpitations. I think an ECG makes sense here, for palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.99,
      "end_seconds": 315.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Ah, um, that's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.76,
      "end_seconds": 342.05,
      "duration_seconds": 24.29,
      "text": "I'll start you on bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day, until review. You take it by mouth. That should help with heart rate control. Cut right back on coffee, tea and energy drinks for now. See me again in three weeks. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.53,
      "end_seconds": 347.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Thank you, you know, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}